Let V be a finite type with decidable equality, let G : SimpleGraph V have decidable adjacency and let hG : G.IsTree. Fix w : V → ℤ and a root ρ : V. Put R := {v : V // v ≠ ρ}, I := {c : V // c ∈ rootedChildren G hG ρ ρ}, C c := rootedChildComponent G ρ c.1, and S := Σ c : I, C c. For every c : I, use the shared local instances Fintype.ofFinite (C c) and the established deleted-edge DecidableRel convention for (C c).toSimpleGraph.Adj. Let e := (rootedChildComponentsEquivNonroot G hG ρ).symm : R ≃ S, D := (rootedGram G w).submatrix Subtype.val Subtype.val, and B c := rootedGram (C c).toSimpleGraph (fun x => w (x : V)).

Assume hChildAdm : ∀ c : I, IsAdmissibleRootedTree (C c).toSimpleGraph (fun x => w (x : V)) (rootedChildRoot G ρ c.1). No ambient assumption IsAdmissibleRootedTree G w ρ is made.

Then the explicitly reindexed inverse is the child block-diagonal inverse:
(Matrix.reindex e.symm e.symm D⁻¹) = Matrix.blockDiagonal' (fun c => (B c)⁻¹).

Consequently, for all c : I and x y : C c,
(Matrix.reindex e.symm e.symm D⁻¹) ⟨c, x⟩ ⟨c, y⟩ = (B c)⁻¹ x y;
for all c d : I, x : C c, and y : C d with c ≠ d,
(Matrix.reindex e.symm e.symm D⁻¹) ⟨c, x⟩ ⟨d, y⟩ = 0;
and for every c : I, at p_c := ⟨c, rootedChildRoot G ρ c.1⟩ : S,
(Matrix.reindex e.symm e.symm D⁻¹) p_c p_c = rootedChildCapacitySummand G hG w ρ c.
